\begin{align*}
	[\partial S]&\in H_{d-1}(W,\mathbb{Z}),\\\dim_{\mathcal{H}}\operatorname{Sing} S\setminus W&\le d-2.
\end{align*}
In other words, $S$ is a relative cycle in $H_d(M,W,\mathbb{Z})$ and the singular set of $S$ outside of $W $ is of Hausdorff dimension at most $(d-2).$

Let $Z$ be another integral current representing $[S].$ 	
	
